messages.content:
Use one JSON file, loaded fully into memory and rewritten on every change.

**Location:** `filepath.Join(os.UserConfigDir(), "books", "books.json")`  
On Linux: `~/.config/books/books.json`, macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/books/books.json`, Windows: `%AppData%\books\books.json`.

**Shape:**

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "books": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "The Go Programming Language",
      "author": "Donovan & Kernighan",
      "status": "reading",
      "page": 42,
      "created_at": "2026-05-07T12:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

Why an object instead of a bare array? You can add fields later without breaking the file.

**Save atomically:**

```go
func save(path string, v any) error {
    b, err := json.MarshalIndent(v, "", "  ")
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }

    dir := filepath.Dir(path)
    tmp, err := os.CreateTemp(dir, "books-*.tmp")
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }
    defer os.Remove(tmp.Name())

    if err := tmp.Chmod(0600); err != nil {
        return err
    }
    if _, err := tmp.Write(b); err != nil {
        return err
    }
    if err := tmp.Sync(); err != nil {
        return err
    }
    if err := tmp.Close(); err != nil {
        return err
    }

    return os.Rename(tmp.Name(), path)
}
```

**Rules:**

- Missing file = empty list.
- Create parent dir with `0700`.
- Write file with `0600`.
- Never truncate/overwrite the real file directly.
- Load once, mutate in memory, save once per command.
- Don’t add locking yet. If you later run multiple instances or store thousands of books, switch to SQLite.

message.content:
Dispatch on `os.Args[1]`, then use a `flag.FlagSet` per subcommand.

```go
func main() {
	if len(os.Args) < 2 {
		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, "usage: books <add|list|update|remove>")
		os.Exit(1)
	}

	var err error
	switch os.Args[1] {
	case "add":
		err = cmdAdd(os.Args[2:])
	default:
		err = fmt.Errorf("unknown command %q", os.Args[1])
	}
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, "error:", err)
		os.Exit(1)
	}
}

func cmdAdd(args []string) error {
	fs := flag.NewFlagSet("add", flag.ExitOnError)
	author := fs.String("author", "", "book author")
	if err := fs.Parse(args); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	title := fs.Arg(0)
	if title == "" {
		return errors.New("add: title required")
	}

	path, err := dataPath()
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	store, err := load(path)
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}

	var maxID int64
	for _, b := range store.Books {
		if b.ID > maxID {
			maxID = b.ID
		}
	}

	store.Books = append(store.Books, Book{
		ID:        maxID + 1,
		Title:     title,
		Author:    *author,
		Status:    StatusReading,
		Page:      0,
		CreatedAt: time.Now().UTC(),
	})

	return save(path, store)
}
```

Usage:

```
books add "The Go Programming Language" --author "Donovan & Kernighan"
```

The flag package requires flags before positional args, so `--author` must come before the title, or switch to `fs.Parse` on reordered args. Simplest fix: quote the title last as shown.
